      "source_line_start": 3257,
      "source_line_end": 3278,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{lemma}[Rational Gap Example for Suprema]\n\\label{lem:rational-gap-suprema}\nLet\n\\[\n  A=\\{q\\in\\mathbb{Q}:q^2<2\\}.\n\\]\nThen $A$ is nonempty and bounded above relative to $\\mathbb{Q}$, but $A$ has\nno supremum in $\\mathbb{Q}$:\n\\[\n  \\nexists s\\in\\mathbb{Q}\\left[\n  (\\forall q\\in A)(q\\leq s)\n  \\land\n  \\forall u\\in\\mathbb{Q}\n  \\bigl((\\forall q\\in A)(q\\leq u)\\Longrightarrow s\\leq u\\bigr)\n  \\right].\n\\]\nWhen $A$ is regarded as a subset of $\\mathbb{R}$, its supremum exists and is\n\\[\n  \\sup_{\\mathbb{R}}A=\\sqrt{2}.\n\\]\n\\hyperref[prf:rational-gap-suprema]{Go to proof.}\n\\end{lemma}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
  "creation_mode": "prompt"
